ConfigureNodes.AZ.description_cn:
Set the availability zone for the node.
The number of nodes in the instance (that is, the `NodeNumber`) and the deployment scheme for the availability zone (that is, the value of the `MultiAZ` parameter) will affect how you fill in this parameter. Details are as follows:

* When creating a single-node instance (that is, `NodeNumber` is set to `1`), only the single-AZ deployment scheme is allowed (that is, `MultiAZ` must be set to `disabled`). In this case, you only need to specify one availability zone in `AZ`, and all nodes in the instance will be deployed in that zone.

For example, if you need to create a single-node instance with all nodes in Availability Zone A, you can use the following configuration:
```JSON
"NodeNumber":1,
"MultiAZ": "disabled",
"ConfigureNodes": [
    {
        "AZ": "cn-beijing-a"
    }
]
```


* When creating a primary/replica instance (that is, `NodeNumber` is greater than or equal to `2`), **the number of availability zones specified must equal the number of nodes per shard** (that is, the value of the `NodeNumber` parameter), and the values for `AZ` must comply with the rules for multi-AZ deployment schemes. The specific rules are as follows:
   * If the primary/replica instance uses a multi-AZ deployment scheme (that is, `MultiAZ` is set to `enabled`), you must specify at least two different availability zone IDs in `AZ`, with the first availability zone being where the primary node is located.
   For example, if you need to create a multi-AZ instance with three nodes per shard, with the primary node in Availability Zone A and the other two replica nodes in Availability Zone C, you can use the following configuration:
   ```JSON
   "NodeNumber":3,
   "MultiAZ": "enabled",
   "ConfigureNodes": [
       {
           "AZ": "cn-beijing-a"
       },
       {
           "AZ": "cn-beijing-c"
       },
       {
           "AZ": "cn-beijing-c"
       }
   ]
   ```

   * If the primary/replica instance uses a single-AZ deployment scheme (that is, `MultiAZ` is set to `disabled`), the availability zone specified for each node must be the same.
   For example, if you need to create a single-AZ instance with three nodes per shard, with all nodes in Availability Zone A, you can use the following configuration:
   ```JSON
   "NodeNumber":3,
   "MultiAZ": "disabled",
   "ConfigureNodes": [
       {
           "AZ": "cn-beijing-a"
       },
       {
           "AZ": "cn-beijing-a"
       },
       {
           "AZ": "cn-beijing-a"
       }
   ]
   ```


You can call the [DescribeZones](https://docs.byteplus.com/en/docs/redis/describezones) API to query the availability zone information in the target region, including the availability zone ID.

